SIDECAR-ONLY (OUT-OF-PROCESS, NOT in uv.lock — C4): the Graphiti closure lives
ONLY in a git-ignored, hash-pinned sidecar venv
(ne.envbuild.ensure_sidecar_venv; graphiti_env/) and is invoked as a SUBPROCESS
uvicorn server over loopback HTTP. None of it enters the platform uv.lock or the
C4 Python license gate (proven by tests/test_no_graph_closure_in_lock.py and the
.importlinter memory-graph-sidecar-out-of-process contract):
graphiti-core / 0.29.2 / Apache-2.0 / https://github.com/getzep/graphiti (sidecar-only)
neo4j (Python driver) / 6.2.0 / Apache-2.0 AND Python-2.0 / https://github.com/neo4j/neo4j-python-driver (sidecar-only)
openai (SDK) / 2.45.0 / Apache-2.0 / https://github.com/openai/openai-python (sidecar-only; ALSO legitimately in the platform lock via litellm — the grep test does NOT assert its absence)
posthog / 7.22.0 / MIT / https://github.com/PostHog/posthog-python (sidecar-only; telemetry FORCE-DISABLED in service.py — C1)

Neo4j Community Edition SERVER / 5.26-community / GPLv3 / https://github.com/neo4j/neo4j
  is a DEV/TEST docker CONTAINER ONLY — never a Python dependency (never in
  uv.lock), never in a customer bundle. The AGE-driver cutover (which drops Neo4j
  CE entirely, running Graphiti on the customer's Apache-2.0 AGE-on-Postgres) is
  NE-083c; Neo4j CE never enters a shipped deployment.

Apache AGE (Apache-2.0) itself (the NE-083c target backend) is a PostgreSQL
EXTENSION loaded into the customer's Postgres (`LOAD 'age'`), not a Python
dependency — it never enters uv.lock or the C4 Python license gate.

psycopg / 3.3.4 / LGPL-3.0-only / https://github.com/psycopg/psycopg
  is the AGE driver's Postgres execution surface, added to the sidecar venv
  (graphiti_env/requirements.txt) by NE-083c. It is sidecar-only HERE, but is ALSO
  legitimately present in the platform uv.lock via ne-brain-graph (the C4 posture was
  settled at NE-081), so tests/test_no_graph_closure_in_lock.py does NOT assert its
  absence and `ne check licenses` needs no policy edit.

The `graphiti_age` driver (graphiti_env/graphiti_age/) is FIRST-PARTY Ryan Junee
code, licensed Apache-2.0 like the rest of the repository. Per the NE-083
Option-B decision it is authored to be separable for contribution upstream to
getzep/graphiti; see docs/architecture/ne083c-graphiti-age-upstream.md.

This package also consumes in-workspace packages (ne-contracts, ne-runtime,
ne-envbuild, ne-audit, ne-events, ne-schema, ne-net, ne-gateway, ne-govern) whose
own third-party components are recorded in their respective NOTICE files. litellm
stays confined to ne.gateway._litellm (the C3 chokepoint is untouched); this
package imports ne-gateway only for the llm_facade's real gateway wiring.
ne-govern supplies the fail-closed redaction stage wired into the llm-facade
gateway (NE-162b); its Presidio backend lives ONLY in ne-govern's isolated
